{"id": "sy-001", "bucket": "synthesis", "question": "Summarize the main supply chain and manufacturing risks Apple discloses.", "filters": {"ticker": "AAPL", "section": "Item 1A"}, "answer_rubric": "A strong answer mentions: reliance on outsourcing/manufacturing partners concentrated in Asia; dependence on single or limited component sources; risk of manufacturing or quality defects; and capacity or production-ramp constraints. Every claim should cite AAPL Item 1A.", "must_cite": [{"ticker": "AAPL", "section": "Item 1A"}], "tags": ["supply_chain"]}
{"id": "sy-002", "bucket": "synthesis", "question": "What risks does NVIDIA face related to customer concentration and demand in the data-center/AI market?", "filters": {"ticker": "NVDA", "section": "Item 1A"}, "answer_rubric": "Should mention concentration among a few large customers, volatility and difficulty forecasting data-center/AI demand, and inventory or purchase-commitment risk from mismatched demand. Should cite NVDA Item 1A.", "must_cite": [{"ticker": "NVDA", "section": "Item 1A"}], "tags": ["concentration", "datacenter"]}
{"id": "sy-003", "bucket": "synthesis", "question": "What credit-related risks does JPMorgan highlight?", "filters": {"ticker": "JPM", "section": "Item 1A"}, "answer_rubric": "Should mention credit risk from consumer and wholesale lending, sensitivity to economic downturns and rising defaults, the allowance for credit losses, and counterparty credit risk. Should cite JPM Item 1A.", "must_cite": [{"ticker": "JPM", "section": "Item 1A"}], "tags": ["credit_risk"]}
{"id": "sy-004", "bucket": "synthesis", "question": "How does Apple describe competition in its markets?", "filters": {"ticker": "AAPL", "section": "Item 1A"}, "answer_rubric": "Should mention highly competitive markets, rapid technological change, aggressive pricing and competitors, and the need to continually innovate and introduce new products. Should cite AAPL Item 1A.", "must_cite": [{"ticker": "AAPL", "section": "Item 1A"}], "tags": ["competition"]}
{"id": "sy-005", "bucket": "synthesis", "question": "Summarize NVIDIA's risks from dependence on third-party manufacturing and supply.", "filters": {"ticker": "NVDA", "section": "Item 1A"}, "answer_rubric": "Should mention reliance on TSMC/foundries and other suppliers, capacity constraints and long lead times, and geopolitical exposure (e.g. concentration in Taiwan). Should cite NVDA Item 1A.", "must_cite": [{"ticker": "NVDA", "section": "Item 1A"}], "tags": ["supply_chain"]}
{"id": "sy-006", "bucket": "synthesis", "question": "What operational and cybersecurity risks does JPMorgan disclose?", "filters": {"ticker": "JPM", "section": "Item 1A"}, "answer_rubric": "Should mention cyberattacks and data breaches, fraud, technology and operational failures, and third-party/vendor risk. Should cite JPM Item 1A.", "must_cite": [{"ticker": "JPM", "section": "Item 1A"}], "tags": ["cyber", "operational"]}
{"id": "sy-007", "bucket": "synthesis", "question": "What does Apple disclose about risks tied to China and its international operations?", "filters": {"ticker": "AAPL", "section": "Item 1A"}, "answer_rubric": "Should mention manufacturing concentration in China, trade tensions and tariffs, political/regulatory risk, and demand sensitivity in Greater China. Should cite AAPL Item 1A.", "must_cite": [{"ticker": "AAPL", "section": "Item 1A"}], "tags": ["china"]}
{"id": "sy-008", "bucket": "synthesis", "question": "Summarize NVIDIA's risks related to U.S. government export controls.", "filters": {"ticker": "NVDA", "section": "Item 1A"}, "answer_rubric": "Should mention U.S. licensing requirements on advanced GPUs, lost or restricted China revenue, compliance complexity, and the unpredictability of new or expanded controls. Should cite NVDA Item 1A.", "must_cite": [{"ticker": "NVDA", "section": "Item 1A"}], "tags": ["export_controls", "china"]}
{"id": "tm-001", "bucket": "temporal", "question": "How has Apple's dedicated cybersecurity-risk disclosure (Item 1C) changed across the fiscal years in scope?", "filters": {"ticker": "AAPL"}, "answer_rubric": "Should note that a dedicated Item 1C (Cybersecurity) appears only for fiscal years ending after Dec 15, 2023 (FY2024 onward), per SEC rule, and that earlier filings in scope lack it. Should cite AAPL Item 1C from FY2024 or FY2025.", "must_cite": [{"ticker": "AAPL", "section": "Item 1C"}], "tags": ["cyber", "temporal"]}
{"id": "tm-002", "bucket": "temporal", "question": "How has NVIDIA's discussion of China export-control risk evolved over its recent fiscal years?", "filters": {"ticker": "NVDA", "section": "Item 1A"}, "answer_rubric": "Should describe escalation over time — expanding license requirements and a growing revenue/impact discussion from earlier to later fiscal years — and cite NVDA Item 1A from more than one fiscal year.", "must_cite": [{"ticker": "NVDA", "section": "Item 1A"}], "tags": ["export_controls", "temporal"]}
{"id": "tm-003", "bucket": "temporal", "question": "Has Apple's characterization of supply-chain concentration risk stayed consistent across the fiscal years in scope?", "filters": {"ticker": "AAPL", "section": "Item 1A"}, "answer_rubric": "Should compare Item 1A language across fiscal years, noting persistent reliance on outsourcing partners concentrated in Asia and single/limited-source components, and cite AAPL Item 1A from at least two fiscal years.", "must_cite": [{"ticker": "AAPL", "section": "Item 1A"}], "tags": ["supply_chain", "temporal"]}
{"id": "tm-004", "bucket": "temporal", "question": "How does JPMorgan's framing of interest-rate and market risk compare across the years in scope?", "filters": {"ticker": "JPM", "section": "Item 1A"}, "answer_rubric": "Should discuss how the rate environment shift (low rates early in the window versus tightening later) is reflected in the risk-factor language, and cite JPM Item 1A from more than one fiscal year.", "must_cite": [{"ticker": "JPM", "section": "Item 1A"}], "tags": ["interest_rate", "temporal"]}
